  "frame_title": "A-trail through three corner-linked squares (two degree-4 vertices)",
  "frame_description": "Three unit squares chained at shared corners: squares A and B meet at vertex 0, squares B and C meet at vertex 5. Both shared vertices have degree 4; every other vertex has degree 2, so the whole graph is Eulerian. A single closed crossing-free circuit weaves through both hubs with non-crossing pairings -- the figure-eight A-trail scaled to a short tessellation strip.",
